= Research data management =

== Overview ==
'''Research data management''' is the planning and practice of organizing, documenting, storing, protecting, preserving, accessing, and sharing research data across its lifecycle.

It covers decisions about formats, metadata, provenance, naming, versioning, storage, backup, access control, preservation, repository selection, licensing, retention, and responsible sharing.

Research data management is broader than data sharing. Some well-managed data may require restricted access because of privacy, ethics, law, security, agreements, or other justified constraints.

== Boundaries ==
* research data management ≠ data sharing only
* managed data ≠ open data necessarily
* backup ≠ long-term preservation

